Lets the core keep the page a switch leaves over the one it shows until that one has drawn (issue
#1438). A page shown again shows only its background until its renderer's first frame, 60 to 230
ms on GitHub's hosted Mac, so the window showed no page partway through every tab and Space switch.
It waits for the renderer's own frame to have been presented, through Blink's ForceRedraw, rather
than for the view's compositor: that one's first frame can come before the page's, and on the Mac
in the same Core Animation transaction as the new layer it draws into, which left a frame of the
background at a switch. A hook only: the core decides what stays, through
content::CallWhenFrameShown.

